<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <!-- No GeneratePackageOnBuild: it conflicts with `dotnet pack` on a multi-targeted Razor class
         library (NU5026/NU5019 from clean) and the documented publish uses `dotnet pack -o ./nupkg`
         then `nuget push nupkg/...`, which never reads the bin/Release package anyway. -->
    <Title>Blazor Controls</Title>
    <PackageId>WssBlazorControls</PackageId>
	  <AssemblyVersion>10.8.1</AssemblyVersion>
	  <FileVersion>$(AssemblyVersion)</FileVersion>
	  <Version>$(AssemblyVersion)</Version>

    <!-- Build hygiene: the changelog promises 0 warnings — enforce it. CS1591 excepted: the public
         surface is heavily XML-documented but not exhaustively, and missing-comment noise would
         drown real warnings. -->
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>

    <!-- Ship the XML docs so consumers get IntelliSense from the package. -->
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>

    <!-- Debuggability + reproducibility: SourceLink is built into the .NET 8+ SDK; publish the
         repo URL, ship a .snupkg symbol package, and make CI builds deterministic. -->
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>

    <!-- Catches binary/source breaking changes against the previous published version at pack time. -->
    <EnablePackageValidation>true</EnablePackageValidation>

    <!-- Trimming / WASM AOT support. IsAotCompatible turns on IsTrimmable (the assembly-level
         [AssemblyMetadata("IsTrimmable","True")] that lets a consumer's trimmed publish actually trim
         this library) plus the trim/AOT/single-file Roslyn analyzers. With TreatWarningsAsErrors
         above, any new IL2xxx/IL3xxx regression fails the build. The reflection the library does
         (attribute reads via Field expressions, enum member lookups) is annotated or provably
         rooted — see EnumHelpers/FieldValidationDisplay for the reasoning. -->
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>

    <!-- Package Metadata -->
    <PackageDescription>A comprehensive library of form controls for Blazor applications, providing consistent, feature-rich input components with built-in validation, accessibility support, and flexible styling options.</PackageDescription>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <!-- SPDX expression (was PackageLicenseFile) so NuGet.org indexes/filters the license properly. -->
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>blazor;controls;forms;validation;accessibility;ui;components;webassembly;server</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
10.8.1 -- a new color control, plus a full accessibility audit of the Edit* form controls (~75 findings) -- the counterpart to 10.8.0's UI-kit audit.

NEW
- EditColor: an AntDesign-5-style color field binding a plain string? -- swatch trigger, saturation/brightness area, hue slider, optional alpha slider, HEX/RGB input row, optional presets. Accepts hex (3/4/6/8-digit) and rgb()/rgba(); emits normalized lowercase hex. Read-only mode shows the swatch itself (plus hex text with ShowText). Backed by the new standalone UI-kit ColorPicker, the public ColorMath helper, and lazily-imported wss-color.js (keyboard and single-click work without JS).
- Localizable accessible-name/announcement parameters across the library: FormLabel.TooltipTriggerLabel + IsRequiredTextIncluded, ReadOnlyValue/EditDisplay EmptyText, EditString show/clear button labels, radio OtherAriaLabel, Select live-region announcement formats + InputLabel/AriaLabelledBy, picker format/range hints and WeekLabel.
- EditDate/EditDateRange gain RangeErrorMessage: an out-of-range typed date now raises a validation message instead of silently reverting (DatePicker.OnRangeError; per-endpoint on DateRangePicker).
- EditFile gains a role="status" live region announcing selection changes, and states its size/count caps up front in the drop zone.

CHANGED
- Auto-generated labels no longer shatter acronyms (URLPath renders "URL Path", not "U R L Path").
- A field's accessible name now comes from its label's text alone (new lbltext-{id} naming anchor) -- a tooltipped field no longer announces "More information" as part of its name.
- EditString's autocomplete fallback infers a real token from the property name (~20 common names) before the one-time-code last resort.
- Contrast: --edit-color-border darkens to clear WCAG 1.4.11's 3:1; new *-strong tokens split text-grade from chrome-grade color uses; edit-controls.css gains its first Windows High Contrast (forced-colors) support.
- EditDate/EditDateRange DialogLabel is now string? -- unset derives the dialog name from the field's own label.

FIXED
- A stale parse/range error on EditDate/EditDateRange now clears when the retyped value equals the one already bound (new OnValidCommit channel on both pickers, per-endpoint on ranges).
- An invalid DatePicker/DateRangePicker field keeps its red error border on hover.
- Select's combobox input now exposes its selected value; option groups now reach assistive tech.

DEPRECATED
- SelectOptionList.Tooltip is [Obsolete] and inert -- it repeated the field's tooltip on every option.

Full changelog: https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls#changelog
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Authors>dcblakesley</Authors>
    <Company>WSS</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2025 WssBlazorControls</Copyright>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Include README and the package icon (license is declared via PackageLicenseExpression) -->
    <None Include="..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <SupportedPlatform Include="browser" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="10.0.10" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
